{{~##
   What every generated Rust file starts with: the banner, the module's own docs, and the
   `use` lines.

   The uses are per file, because an unused one is a warning and the crate root does not
   silence that - so each file is handed exactly what its own text reaches for, from
   TypeDependencies. `crate::` rather than `super::`, so a file does not care how deep the
   module tree around it is.

   `module_doc` is for the file whose whole contents are the subject - a constant set, where
   there is no item for a `///` to attach to. Inner doc comments have to come before any item,
   which is why this goes above the uses rather than beside the thing it describes.

   The lints are set once in lib.rs, at crate scope, so nothing here repeats them.
##~}}
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Generated by Tabbit. DO NOT EDIT.
//
// Changes to this file may cause incorrect behavior and will be lost if the code is
// regenerated.
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
{{~ if module_doc | array.size > 0 }}
{{~ for line in module_doc ~}}
//! {{ line }}
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ if uses | array.size > 0 }}
{{~ for line in uses ~}}
{{ line }}
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ end ~}}

